Flnc2 external tools
====================

This archive contains third-party software and data used by Flnc2 to assess
the coding potential of candidate transcripts. Flnc2 downloads it on first
use; it is not part of the Flnc2 source code. Each component remains under
the terms of its original authors. If you use Flnc2 in published work,
please also cite the tools below.

Files are redistributed unmodified.


1. CPAT: Coding-Potential Assessment Tool
-----------------------------------------
Files:     cpat/Human_Hexamer.tsv
           cpat/Human_logitModel.RData
           cpat/Human_cutoff.txt
           cpat/Mouse_Hexamer.tsv
           cpat/Mouse_logitModel.RData
           cpat/Mouse_cutoff.txt
           cpat/LICENSE
Version:   3.0.5
Source:    https://sourceforge.net/projects/rna-cpat/
License:   GNU General Public License version 2.0 (GPLv2); see cpat/LICENSE.
           The CPAT program itself is installed separately (bioconda: cpat).
Citation:  Wang L, Park HJ, Dasari S, Wang S, Kocher JP, Li W.
           CPAT: Coding-Potential Assessment Tool using an alignment-free
           logistic regression model.
           Nucleic Acids Research. 2013;41(6):e74. doi:10.1093/nar/gkt006


